From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 7 Jun 2026 21:08:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00869/11171] [outer-loop] Step-level process-reward SCOPED +
 de-risk PASSES (outcome AUROC 0.73)

Scopes the most-promising rescue path (dense per-step process-reward, not hard trace
certification) + runs its gating de-risk. RESULT: aggregated per-step process-reward
ranks correct traces above incorrect at trace-outcome AUROC 0.73 (fraction_certified;
mean 0.72) on 558 free-form p01 traces -- GATE PASSES (>=0.65). The soft/dense reward
keeps the per-step signal that the HARD all-clean certification (56%, Phase 0) threw
away. So verifier-as-self-improvement-reward is VIABLE via process-reward (not hard
RFT certification): use the verifier as a DENSE reward. Build now justified: process-
reward-weighted SFT on a 0.5B base (fine-tune harness = the remaining gap). Caveats:
0.73 moderate (process-vs-outcome + OOD attenuation), correlational not causal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
